WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.080
Not all Star Wars rumors are created equal.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.779
Many of the ideas out there for Episode IX,
while fun to consider, are just too outlandish

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:09.450
to stand a chance at being real.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.740
Other rumors, though, sound all too plausible
— and that's not necessarily a good thing.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.420
One new report making the rounds is raising
serious concerns among franchise fans, getting

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.779
people worried that the saga-concluding sequel
might just be a tired rehash of Return of

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:23.779
the Jedi.

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:29.429
According to a report popularized by YouTuber
Mike Zeroh, Episode 9 will include a gigantic,

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.789
planet-destroying weapon —yes, again.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:35.670
The rumor hinges around a purportedly leaked
scene description from the untitled ninth

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:40.740
Star Wars episode, which goes into detail
about the attributes of the supposed superweapon.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.000
The scene reportedly centers on Kylo Ren,
now the Supreme Leader of the villainous First

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.840
Order, sitting in a room at what seems to
be the organization's headquarters.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:53.550
He's said to be analyzing a hologram displaying
a yet-to-be-completed array of superweapons.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.440
According to the leak, the son of Han and
Leia will be seen sizing up three weapons

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.710
shaped like cylinders with large engines,
blasting blue and red energy, watching as

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.860
they destroy the terrain of an unknown world.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.039
While the weapon appears capable of immense
destructive power, it also seems to still

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.280
be under construction.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.400
Sound familiar?

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:15.180
Some have noted that the rumored weapon sounds
strikingly similar to a World Devastator,

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:19.520
which is a form of technology featured in
the old Star Wars expanded universe — particularly

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.120
the Star Wars Legends "Dark Empire" storyline.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:27.020
Designed by Imperial engineers who helped
craft the original Death Star, the World Devastators

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:31.070
are described as weapons that land on planets
and use tractor beam technology to rip the

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:34.069
land apart, decimating everything in their
reach.

00:01:34.069 --> 00:01:38.219
While the Death Stars were incredibly effective
mass-killing machines, the World Devastators

00:01:38.219 --> 00:01:42.340
take things one step further by extracting
the rubble from destroyed planets.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:47.149
The weapon ships, armed to the teeth with
guns, lasers, missiles, ion cannons, and more,

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:51.290
would harvest the remnants of ravaged worlds
for fuel and resources, which would then be

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.939
used to power the ships' engines.

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:57.310
The salvaged material also would also serve
as fuel for the ships' internal foundries,

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:01.429
which were used to create more cruisers, droids,
and destructive weapons.

00:02:01.429 --> 00:02:05.789
While the World Devastators aren't currently
a part of Disney's revived Star Wars canon,

00:02:05.789 --> 00:02:09.730
there's nothing stopping Episode IX director
J.J. Abrams from digging through the series'

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:13.090
history books and bringing past elements back
into the fold.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:17.080
But just because it's plausible doesn't mean
that fans want to see it happen on screen.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.570
If the new movie really does feature yet another
giant weapon based on Death Star tech, it

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:25.760
would feel remarkably similar to Return of
the Jedi, not to mention the original Star

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.540
Wars movie, or The Force Awakens.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.060
While that seventh Star Wars episode, also
directed by Abrams, was praised for how it

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:37.070
reignited that classic Star Wars after years'
worth of weird prequels, many rolled their

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:42.380
eyes at the inclusion of Starkiller Base — a
bigger, badder Death Star in everything but

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:42.880
name.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.340
After the divisive response to The Last Jedi,
which tried to take the series in some controversial

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:51.980
new directions, as well as the muted reaction
to the Han Solo spinoff, it's possible that

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:56.260
Disney and Lucasfilm will want to play things
safe for the series' ninth episode.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.590
Maybe the idea is to go back to what worked
before, instead of risk alienating people

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:01.840
again with something new.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:06.180
But as the fan reaction to the rumor seems
to indicate, there is such a thing as being

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:06.960
too familiar.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:11.560
Some people are even making arguments in support
of the prequel movies, which at the very least

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:15.000
seemed to try new things, even though they
didn't always stick the landing.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:19.210
To many viewers, Star Wars should be about
more than just laser swords, Death Stars,

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.080
and Darth Vader.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.500
Going back to that well too many times seems
to speak to a lack of imagination, and even

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.760
risks turning people off the series for good.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.040
But is this rumor true?

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.620
We don't know, but it feels believable, and
that's what has fans worried.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:36.780
Star Wars is supposed to offer a whole galaxy
of ideas, not just the same one, over and

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:37.280
over.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:42.220
It's hard to imagine anyone being satisfied
with another superweapon serving up the climax

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.060
of the decade-spanning Skywalker Saga.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:49.120
There's no way Episode 9 will satisfy everybody,
but can't it at least try to surprise us?

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:49.800
We can only hope.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.319
We'll find out for sure what's going down
when the movie hits theaters on December 20th,

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:55.079
2019.

